(Non-blocking reap (WNOHANG) returns 0 while a child is still running,
 then the child's PID after it exits - the whole value of the form. The
 parent forks a child that sleeps 30 seconds, reaps without waiting -
 which must be 0, nothing finished yet, and not an error - and checks
 the reaped status is still the -1 sentinel, because a reap that reaps
 nothing must not disturb it. Then it SIGKILLs the child, lets it settle
 into a zombie, and reaps without waiting again, which must return the
 child's pid. The pid is variable, so it is checked against the forked
 child's pid rather than printed.)

Set pid to fork the process.
If pid is 0 then,
    Wait 30 seconds.
If pid is greater than 0 then,
    a number called 'status before any reap' is the reaped status,
    Set 'reap result' to reap child pid without waiting,
    a number called 'status after nonblocking reap' is the reaped status,
    Print "before any reap: {'status before any reap'}",
    Print "first reap child alive: {'reap result'}",
    Print "status after nonblocking reap: {'status after nonblocking reap'}",
    Send signal 9 to process pid,
    Wait 100 milliseconds,
    Set 'reap result' to reap child pid without waiting,
    If 'reap result' is pid then,
        Print "second reap returned child pid".